act immutable CR bytes. The normative authority is the pinned internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md Sections 11.10, 11.10.1-11.10.5, 11.9, 11.2/11.3, 15.1/15.3 and the Section 7.5 LeaseToken; the credential owner is internal/hosttrust as accepted in CR-TASK-260909-2ez769-12 (verdict TASK-260909-2ez769_review-verdict-rev12.md).\n2|\n3|Verify with your own instruments: (1) Restoration — recompute sha256 for every packet file against manifest.json and against the candidate's internal/rpcwire files at the restoration point recorded (the producer states 10 of 11 restored verbatim then extended; UNRESOLVED_QUESTIONS.md dropped as superseded — judge whether dropping it is faithful given the resolution note on the task); confirm the four hand-re-applied tracked deltas (README, ownership gap texts, projection digest, config fuzz gate) carry no self-minted coverage change (coverage levels and clause enumerations unchanged, digest recomputed independently). (2) Section 11.10.1 conformance with real TLS — using in-memory duplex streams and certificates issued through the landed hosttrust issuance path (Section 11.10.2 profile), drive hostchannel.Dial/Serve/Call yourself: positive full handshake + hello + one RPC-5 operation in both roles; then the refusal table with your own vectors — TLS 1.2-only client, missing ALPN and a wrong ALPN string, a session-ticket/PSK/0-RTT attempt (assert SessionTicketsDisabled and a nil client cache take effect: a second connection must not resume), a plaintext preface byte before TLS, ServerName set to the SSH endpoint instead of the UUID SAN, a leaf with a second SAN, an unenrolled root, a revoked leaf, a retiring entry past retire_at, an expired leaf, the system pool, hello host ID mismatch on client and on server, destination mismatch on the client, a valid non-hello request before hello, an invalid hello, a stale authorization generation at dispatch and at a mutation boundary (rotate/revoke through hosttrust between hello and the call), oversize handshake bytes (state where Go's 256 KiB message cap fires versus the 1 MiB unit cap), a silent peer past the 10-second handshake deadline (use a shortened deadline hook if the package exposes one; otherwise run the real deadline once), hello past its deadline, an oversize hello line (8 MiB) and object (5 MiB); for each assert the exact Error 1.3.0 class and exit (host_identity_mismatch/peer_not_allowlisted 7, incompatible_protocol 6 only when known, authentication_failed 7, transport_failure 8, invalid_config 3), that at most one encrypted error frame precedes close, that nothing but a TLS alert leaves before handshake completion, and that no new Error enum or exit code exists (diff internal/axerror against trunk). (3) HC-* gates — for every gate in the matrix run the producer's positive/negative vectors and add one vector of your own per gate; confirm HC-MIGRATE selects Host Channel 1 + RPC 5 only from a Config-4 document and refuses a legacy hello route; HC-GENERATION: dispatch and every mutation boundary consult hosttrust.AuthorizeDispatch/WithMutationAuthorization with the current committed generation (plant a call that bypasses the boundary — the census must refuse); HC-EXCLUDE: static + runtime write censuses prove no durable write and no key/exporter/secret persistence (plant a write and a KeyLogWriter assignment — both must be refused); HC-PARITY: the Stream abstraction has no SSH-implementation branch (grep and a plant). (4) RPC 5.0.0 wire — RPC-4 operations/envelopes/8 namespaces/limits/25-key hello unchanged except protocol_version 5.0.0 and contracts.rpc [\"5.0.0\"]; diff the v4 and v5 fixtures; confirm Structured Error stays statically 1.3.0 for majors 4 and 5 through the new axerror binding row; run the fuzz target 200x. (5) Mutation — rerun both harnesses (hostchannel 22 narrowing + neutral + documented client-cache SURVIVED; rpcwire 34 narrowing) in an isolated copy, rerun each KILLED twice, examine the documented SURVIVED (client-cache) and decide whether a behavioral test can kill it (a second Dial must not resume — write it), plant at least four narrowing mutants of your own on arms the producer did not mutate (ALPN compare by prefix; ServerName check skipped when the SAN count is 1; generation compare `>=`; hello UUID compare case-insensitive) plus an applied harmless SURVIVED control; per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, precise denominators. (6) AC accounting — the seven original rows are now claimed 7 of 7 through the authenticated runtime consumer: confirm each row's named test reaches the production entry through a real TLS-authenticated channel, not a stub. (7) Docs, config and hygiene — README/LOGBOOK make no capability claim (no ax command, no SSH launch, no provider plugin, no object exchange); the task-board.config.json change is exactly one added fuzz-gate command (JSON-walk the diff; no other field) and that command passes on the candidate; changed_paths carry no __pycache__/.pyc/stray plants; gofmt/vet clean; go test ./internal/rpcwire ./internal/hostchannel ./internal/hosttrust ./internal/axerror ./internal/traceability/... -count=1 and -race green; tracecheck and cataloggen -check exit 0 on the exact tree.\n4|\n5|Method: isolated immutable probes only, never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; never modify the preserved packet; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration; Curator go-testing-tools skill; all CI local; PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 for every harness; keep scratch small under .temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/ and delete candidate copies when done. Attach TASK-260830-z1yxg9_review-verdict-rev1.md and TASK-260830-z1yxg9_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), complete the live merged checklist, then accept_cr(TASK-260830-z1yxg9, revision=1, evidence=TASK-260830-z1yxg9_review-verdict-rev1.md) or hand off changes requested with P1/P2/P3 classes named. Model: muse-spark xhigh (codex reviewers are out of quota until 2026-09-19). Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.cu