utate (ALPN compare by prefix; ServerName check skipped when the SAN count is 1; generation compare `>=`; hello UUID compare case-insensitive) plus an applied harmless SURVIVED control; per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, precise denominators. (6) AC accounting — the seven original rows are now claimed 7 of 7 through the authenticated runtime consumer: confirm each row's named test reaches the production entry through a real TLS-authenticated channel, not a stub. (7) Docs, config and hygiene — README/LOGBOOK make no capability claim (no ax command, no SSH launch, no provider plugin, no object exchange); the task-board.config.json change is exactly one added fuzz-gate command (JSON-walk the diff; no other field) and that command passes on the candidate; changed_paths carry no __pycache__/.pyc/stray plants; gofmt/vet clean; go test ./internal/rpcwire ./internal/hostchannel ./internal/hosttrust ./internal/axerror ./internal/traceability/... -count=1 and -race green; tracecheck and cataloggen -check exit 0 on the exact tree.\n4|\n5|Method: isolated immutable probes only, never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; never modify the preserved packet; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration; Curator go-testing-tools skill; all CI local; PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 for every harness; keep scratch small under .temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/ and delete candidate copies when done. Attach TASK-260830-z1yxg9_review-verdict-rev1.md and TASK-260830-z1yxg9_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), complete the live merged checklist, then accept_cr(TASK-260830-z1yxg9, revision=1, evidence=TASK-260830-z1yxg9_review-verdict-rev1.md) or hand off changes requested with P1/P2/P3 classes named. Model: muse-spark xhigh (codex reviewers are out of quota until 2026-09-19). Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
